Problem URL - https://leetcode.com/problems/rising-temperature/description/?envType=study-plan-v2&envId=top-sql-50

Solution Logic - Use a self join on Weather table and then find the difference between the dates if equal to 1, then check if the temperature of table 1 is greater than table 2

Solution - 

SELECT w1.id
FROM Weather w1, Weather w2
WHERE DATEDIFF(w1.recordDate, w2.recordDate) = 1
AND w1.temperature > w2.temperature


Pyspark solution  - 
from pyspark.sql.types import *
from pyspark.sql.functions import *
from pyspark.sql.window import Window
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession

spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("Rising Temperature").getOrCreate()

joined_df = df_weather.alias("w1").join(
    df_weather.alias("w2"),
    expr("DATEDIFF(w1.recordDate, w2.recordDate) = 1 AND w1.temperature > w2.temperature"),
    "inner"  # Use inner join to filter based on the condition
)

joined_df.select(col("w1.id")).show()